{
  "id": "read-dashboard-panels-lj-preview",
  "title": "Read a dashboard panel",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "Practise the ideas from section 2 of Introduction to dashboards. Identify a panel's question, find its queries and data sources, connect its unit setting to the displayed values, and choose measurements for a resource or service."
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "Use the finished dashboards on Grafana Play. The examples include demo data; don't treat their values as operational limits. Inspect settings without saving changes."
    },
    { "type": "markdown", "content": "You'll connect a panel's title, value, and scale to the question it answers." },
    { "type": "section", "id": "read-memory", "title": "Read the Memory panel", "blocks": [
      { "type": "interactive", "action": "navigate", "reftarget": "/d/3SWXxreWk/grafana-dashboard?viewPanel=22&from=now-1h&to=now&timezone=browser", "verify": "on-page:/d/3SWXxreWk", "content": "Open the **Memory** gauge on **Grafana Dashboard**." },
      { "type": "markdown", "content": "Find the number and its B suffix. Follow the filled arc around the gauge. Notice that the panel shows one value within a range, not its changes over time." },
      { "type": "markdown", "content": "The **Memory** panel answers \"How much memory is in use on average over the selected period?\" Its value is a mean and its unit is bytes. Its configured range is a demo setting, not a real server's capacity." }
    ] },
    { "type": "markdown", "content": "You've identified what the panel measures and how it summarizes the selected period. Next, inspect where a panel gets its data." },
    { "type": "markdown", "content": "You'll inspect two queries that supply data to the same panel without changing their expressions." },
    { "type": "section", "id": "inspect-queries", "title": "Find the panel's data sources", "blocks": [
      { "type": "interactive", "action": "navigate", "reftarget": "/d/000000100/mixed-datasources?from=now-24h&to=now&timezone=browser", "verify": "on-page:/d/000000100", "content": "Open the **Mixed Datasources** dashboard." },
      { "type": "interactive", "action": "highlight", "reftarget": "[data-viz-panel-key='panel-1'] button[data-testid='data-testid Panel menu Prometheus and Loki']", "requirements": ["on-page:/d/000000100", "exists-reftarget"], "doIt": false, "tooltip": "Click here to open the panel menu, then select Edit.", "content": "Open the **Prometheus and Loki** panel menu and select **Edit**. Select query **A** if it isn't already selected." },
      { "type": "interactive", "action": "highlight", "reftarget": "input[data-testid='data-testid Select a data source']", "requirements": ["on-page:/d/000000100", "exists-reftarget"], "doIt": false, "content": "Notice the Prometheus data source for query **A**." },
      { "type": "markdown", "content": "Query **A** gets metrics from Prometheus. The data source tells you where Grafana sends the query; the query selects and summarizes data for the panel." },
      { "type": "interactive", "action": "button", "reftarget": "[role='button'][aria-label='Select card C']", "requirements": ["on-page:/d/000000100", "exists-reftarget"], "doIt": true, "content": "Select query **C** to inspect the panel's second query." },
      { "type": "interactive", "action": "highlight", "reftarget": "input[data-testid='data-testid Select a data source']", "requirements": ["on-page:/d/000000100", "exists-reftarget"], "doIt": false, "content": "Notice the Loki data source for query **C**." },
      { "type": "markdown", "content": "Query **C** gets logs from Grafana Loki and calculates values from them. The panel's **Mixed** data source lets its queries use different sources. The panel displays results from both queries." },
      { "type": "markdown", "content": "A query's result format doesn't lock it to one visualization. Timestamped numeric samples can form a time-series graph or supply a summary value to a stat or gauge. Choose the display for the question, then make sure the query returns the fields it needs." },
      { "type": "interactive", "action": "navigate", "reftarget": "/d/000000100/mixed-datasources?viewPanel=1&from=now-24h&to=now&timezone=browser", "verify": "on-page:/d/000000100", "content": "Return to the panel without saving editor changes." }
    ] },
    { "type": "markdown", "content": "You've found a panel's queries and traced each one to its data source. The visualization presents their results; it doesn't define where the data comes from." },
    { "type": "markdown", "content": "You'll locate the unit setting and connect it to the suffix on the Memory gauge." },
    { "type": "section", "id": "inspect-unit", "title": "Connect the setting to the label", "blocks": [
      { "type": "interactive", "action": "navigate", "reftarget": "/d/3SWXxreWk/grafana-dashboard?viewPanel=22&from=now-1h&to=now&timezone=browser", "verify": "on-page:/d/3SWXxreWk", "content": "Open the **Memory** gauge and notice the B suffix beside its value." },
      { "type": "markdown", "content": "Open the **Memory** panel menu and select **Edit**. Expand **Standard options** if it's collapsed. Leave the settings unchanged." },
      { "type": "interactive", "action": "highlight", "reftarget": "#unit", "requirements": ["on-page:/d/3SWXxreWk", "exists-reftarget"], "doIt": false, "content": "Find **Unit** and read its **bytes(IEC)** setting." },
      { "type": "markdown", "content": "The **Memory** panel formats its numeric value as bytes. B means bytes; larger values can use units such as KiB or MiB. Unit formatting changes the display, not the query's data, and doesn't change timestamps into byte values." },
      { "type": "interactive", "action": "highlight", "reftarget": "[id='reduceOptions.calcs']", "requirements": ["on-page:/d/3SWXxreWk", "exists-reftarget"], "doIt": false, "content": "Find **Calculation** under **Value options** and notice **Mean**." },
      { "type": "markdown", "content": "**Mean** chooses the average of the samples. **Unit** formats that average. Changing the unit to percent wouldn't calculate memory utilization; the query would first need to return a proportion of capacity." },
      { "type": "interactive", "action": "navigate", "reftarget": "/d/3SWXxreWk/grafana-dashboard?viewPanel=22&from=now-1h&to=now&timezone=browser", "verify": "on-page:/d/3SWXxreWk", "content": "Return to the **Memory** gauge without saving changes." }
    ] },
    { "type": "markdown", "content": "You've located Unit and distinguished formatting from calculation. Read the label and the query together before interpreting a value." },
    { "type": "markdown", "content": "You'll apply the measurement methods from section 2 to two different dashboard goals." },
    { "type": "section", "id": "match-measurements", "title": "Choose resource and service measurements", "blocks": [
      { "type": "markdown", "content": "Start with the resource question \"Is this machine running out of memory?\" The Memory gauge shows bytes, but bytes alone don't tell you the available capacity or whether work is waiting." },
      { "type": "markdown", "content": "Use USE for the resource: utilization shows how much capacity is busy, saturation shows work that can't be served immediately, and errors show failures. For memory, pair used capacity with evidence of memory pressure or waiting work and allocation failures." },
      { "type": "markdown", "content": "Now use the service question \"Are checkout requests failing or slowing down?\" Match it to RED: request rate shows demand, errors show failures, and duration shows how long requests take. A memory panel alone can't answer this user-facing question." },
      { "type": "markdown", "content": "The four golden signals cover the same service concerns as traffic, errors, and latency, then add saturation. To connect symptoms with capacity, add a relevant saturation measure, such as a growing queue, rather than assuming high traffic means overload." },
      { "type": "markdown", "content": "For a dashboard you use, name its resource or service question. Identify one measure it needs and whether the viewer needs its latest value or its change over time. That choice determines both the query and the visualization." }
    ] },
    { "type": "markdown", "content": "You've connected a panel's question, query, unit, and measurement method. Continue to section 3 to practise choosing how to display those measurements." }
  ]
}